        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported skin spots and symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Multiple rough spots on hands, forearms, and face for months; mostly asymptomatic until the last few weeks, with intermittent itch and irritation, especially with gloves or a hat. No pain, bleeding, ulceration, or systemic symptoms reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Typical actinic keratosis-type lesions on exposed skin"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dozens of 2–6 mm erythematous rough scaly macules and papules on the dorsal hands, forearms, forehead, temples, and ears; sandpaper feel; non-tender, with no induration, ulceration, or bleeding. Examination was limited to the face, scalp, neck, forearms, and hands."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
